      "title": "2027 Cardinal Transition Coordinator",
      "description": "PeopleAdmin Applicant Portal | 2027 Cardinal Transition Coordinator Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities at North Central College Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help 2027 Cardinal Transition Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Federal Work Study Eligible? Yes Posting Number ST001074 Position Title 2027 Cardinal Transition Coordinator Department Student Success Division Academic Affairs Supervisor Linh Phu Supervisor Title Assistant Director of Student Success Description of Job Duties · Assist in planning, preparation, and implementation of transition programs such as Placement Testing, Advising & Registration, Orientation Week, and First-Year Experience programs · Support the recruitment and selection of additional student staff to support all the transition programs · Help plan and execute a training program for transition staff · Assist with the evaluation and assessment of the transition programs · Manage emails, data, and schedules for different programs as assigned · Help create and distribute marketing materials · Work collaboratively with all campus partners to support the transition programs · Welcome new students and their families to the North Central College Community · Complete tasks by deadlines as assigned · Serve as a role model/mentor for new students and transition staff · Serve as a point of contact for the transition programs · Present information on campus resources to new students, parents, and transition staff · Maintain a positive environment · Attend all training, Placement Testing, Advising & Registration, and Orientation Week events as assigned · Support transition staff during assigned summer hours · Communicate with off-campus vendors · Work 10-15 mutually agreed-upon hours per week during Spring 2027 semester, approximately 30 hours per week during the summer, and approximately 2-4 hours per week in Fall 2027. This position would also work as needed in Fall 2026 to prepare for spring orientation. · Able to serve as a self-motivated leader and to take initiative when appropriate Do the job duties for this position include any driving requirements? No Job Qualifications · Cumulative Grade Point Average of 3.0 and in good judicial standing · Enrolled as a full-time undergraduate student at North Central College in the Fall 2026, Spring 2027, and Fall 2027 Semesters · Campus leadership experience · Demonstrate knowledge of campus resources or willingness to learn · Prior orientation/transition experience required (at North Central or another school, if transfer student) · *May not participate in any Cardinal Destination Courses Abroad (May Term trip) Will this position be working with minors? No Approximate number of work hours per week Varies Posting Detail Information EEO Statement North Central College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. North Central College provides reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities where appropriate. If you need reasonable accommodation, please notify the Office of Human Resource. Determinations on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. Open Date 10/07/2026 Close Date 10/16/2026 Open Until Filled No Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Why do you think you are the best person for the Cardinal Transition Coordinator position? (Open Ended Question) * What is one lesson you learned from your previous orientation experience that you will apply to this role? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents North Central College 30 North Brainard Street, Naperville, IL 60540 630.637.5757 humanresources@hr.noctrl.edu . Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
