    "https://northcentralcollege.peopleadmin.com/postings/15918": {
      "title": "Student Gallery Assistant, Dept. of Art &amp; Design",
      "description": "PeopleAdmin Applicant Portal | Student Gallery Assistant, Dept. of Art &amp; Design Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities at North Central College Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Student Gallery Assistant, Dept. of Art & Design Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Federal Work Study Eligible? Yes Posting Number ST000981 Position Title Student Gallery Assistant, Dept. of Art & Design Department College of Arts & Sciences Division Academic Affairs Supervisor Kathryn Pszotka Supervisor Title Director of Campus Galleries & Coordinator of First Year Experience Description of Job Duties North Central College is hiring Student Gallery Assistants to staff open hours at the Schoenherr Gallery in the Wentz Fine Arts Center, as well as exhibition preparation & execution for two additional gallery venues on campus. Responsibilities • Welcome and engage with gallery patrons, ensuring a positive, accessible experience • Answer patron questions and share information about current exhibitions • Monitor gallery space to ensure artwork security • Support special events and exhibition preparation • Assist install & deinstall exhibits: loading artwork in and out of campus galleries (Schoenherr, Oesterle, and Meiley-Swallow, as needed), posting marketing information around campus, clerical tasks, gallery maintenance, etc. • Prepare and support both current & future shows through marketing, social media, research, light maintenance & cleaning duties, etc. Expectations • Work independently with minimal supervision • Communicate clearly and reliably with co-workers, patrons, and supervisors Open to students of all majors interested in gaining experience in curatorial practice, educational programming, and nonprofit management Must be available regular hours with minimum schedule changes. Everyone will work a minimum of 5 hours each week but should be available a minimum of 10 hours each week to allow for staffing needs. Special projects and additional hours frequently available. Do the job duties for this position include any driving requirements? No Job Qualifications Must be: o enrolled as a student at North Central College o available a minimum of 10 hours of availability and intend to work for at least 5 each week. o available one Saturday a month o available for a minimum of one special event per month Will this position be working with minors? No Approximate number of work hours per week 5-7 hours on average. Depends on individual & team availability as well as overall Schoenherr gallery hours. Gallery hours (open) are mid-morning through early evening M-SA with special events a few times a semester. Looking for assistance during the summ Posting Detail Information EEO Statement North Central College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. NCC provides reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities where appropriate. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application or hiring process, please notify the Office of Human Resources at 630-637-5757 or humanresources@hr.noctrl.edu Determinations for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. Open Date 08/01/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you feel comfortable using Microsoft software (Word, Excel, Team, etc.), Canva, and the Google Suit tools? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have experience creating or managing social media content? (Open Ended Question) * Are you comfortable lifting a minimum of 25 pounds in order to safely assist in exhibit preparation? Accommodations are available, and the answer will not affect hiring decisions. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Optional Documents North Central College 30 North Brainard Street, Naperville, IL 60540 630.637.5757 humanresources@hr.noctrl.edu . Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
