    "https://northcentralcollege.peopleadmin.com/postings/15508": {
      "title": "Adjunct Pool for Physician Assistant Studies (MSPAS)",
      "description": "PeopleAdmin Applicant Portal | Adjunct Pool for Physician Assistant Studies (MSPAS) Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities at North Central College Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Adjunct Pool for Physician Assistant Studies (MSPAS) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F000415 Position Title Adjunct Pool for Physician Assistant Studies (MSPAS) Department Physician Assistant Studies Division Academic Affairs Faculty Status Part time Faculty Supervisor Title Program Director of MS Physician Assistant Studies Status Per Course Part-time Faculty Tenure Track No Salary Range Varies depending on the course Position Summary The MSPAS Program at North Central College invites applications to teach courses as a faculty associate during the 2025-2026 academic year. The successful candidate will teach one to two MSPAS courses or lab assistant per semester. The role requires someone who is a board-certified physician assistant (PA-C) or physician (MD), with experience in graduate physician assistant student education. A viable candidate can deliver course content, contribute to the creation of assignments and other assessments, evaluate and grade student work, and hold office hours to assist students. MSPAS faculty associate (adjunct) appointments are on a course-by-course basis. This posting is continuous to develop a qualified pool of interested candidates. If your academic area of interest/expertise meets our programmatic needs at any time, you may be contacted to discuss teaching opportunities. These needs change from semester to semester. The position is a non-benefits eligible, fixed-term appointment with no tenure eligibility. The number of courses is contingent upon unit needs, funding, and sufficient enrollment. Minimum Required Qualifications: · Master’s degree in physician assistant studies or MD · Unincumbered Illinois License · All degrees must be from an accredited institution. A terminal degree is preferred. Preferred Qualifications: · Prior higher education teaching experience preferred · Experience facilitating student-led classroom discussions · Evidence of working with a diverse student population · Evidence of effective collaboration skills · Experience with technology/course management systems (e.g. Canvas) · Excellent written and verbal English communication skills The review of applications will occur as the School has needs for a particular course . Applications will continue to be accepted and reviewed on an ongoing basis. This pool recruitment will be live throughout the academic year, and the School may or may not hire from it, depending on course needs. A background check and official transcripts are required prior to employment. Employment Conditions An offer of employment is contingent upon successful completion of the College’s background screening process. Number of Vacancies 1 Posting Detail Information EEO Statement North Central College is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to increasing the diversity of our workforce. North Central College provides reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities where appropriate. If you need reasonable accommodation, please notify the Office of Human Resource. Determinations on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Additional Information The salary range for adjuncts in the Physican Assistant Studies Program (Master of Science) program can range from $2970 to $15,000, depending on the course. The pay offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors including (but not limited to) the selected candidate’s experience and qualifications, including equivalent years in rank, training, and field or discipline; internal equity; and external market pay for comparable jobs. Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you authorized to work in the US? YES NO * Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for work authorization? YES NO Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Unofficial Graduate Transcripts North Central College 30 North Brainard Street, Naperville, IL 60540 630.637.5757 humanresources@hr.noctrl.edu . Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://northcentralcollege.peopleadmin.com/postings/15494": {
      "title": "Tutor-Student Worker",
      "description": "PeopleAdmin Applicant Portal | Tutor-Student Worker Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities at North Central College Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Tutor-Student Worker Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Federal Work Study Eligible? Yes Posting Number ST001023 Position Title Tutor-Student Worker Department Student Success Division Academic Affairs Supervisor Jacquelyn Binger Supervisor Title Academic Success and Support Services Specialist Description of Job Duties Student tutors work with their peers to discuss content information in particular courses in the Library Learning Commons. Tutors only tutor by appointment. Applicants are strongly encouraged to tutor multiple courses/subject areas, and will be asked to indicate particular courses they feel most comfortable to tutor. Tutor Primary Activities: Aid students with content information and provide study strategy assistance for students who seek assistance. Maintain appropriate professional attitudes and behaviors to staff, students, and others. Participate in all scheduled tutor meetings and complete mandatory training prior to the first tutoring session. Other duties as assigned by supervisor. Training New and re-hired employees must complete all onboarding tasks assigned by HR before they can begin working. Training will be provided and is mandatory for all student tutors. Training will be paid at the position’s hourly rate. Students who do not complete training as scheduled, will not continue working in the position. Do the job duties for this position include any driving requirements? No Job Qualifications Tutor Qualifications: Current NCC student with an overall GPA of 3.0 or above is required. A grade of 3.0 or above in the tutor’s selected course(s) is preferred; prior enrollment with the professor who is to teach the selected course is preferred. Content-competency required. Good interpersonal and communication skills required. Application Requirements Upload a resume and cover letter to this online application. If you need assistance in the creation of a resume or cover letter, please contact the Center for Career and Professional Development at career@noctrl.edu or 630-637-5141. The NCC faculty reference will receive an email request with a link to upload their statement testifying to your competency in the faculty’s subject area. Applications without this faculty reference will be considered incomplete and not qualified. Applicants are required to complete a short interview with the tutoring supervisor or supporting staff. Will this position be working with minors? No Approximate number of work hours per week 15 Posting Detail Information EEO Statement North Central College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. NCC provides reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities where appropriate. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application or hiring process, please notify the Office of Human Resources at 630-637-5757 or humanresources@hr.noctrl.edu Determinations for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. Open Date 07/18/2022 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please select the answer that best describes your student work authorization: I am authorized to work for any US employer and can provide documentation, if hired. I am an international student with a US social security number authorized for campus work. I am an international student and will need to apply for a US social security number, if hired. I cannot provide US work authorization. * Are you currently enrolled as a North Central College student? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation 1 North Central College 30 North Brainard Street, Naperville, IL 60540 630.637.5757 humanresources@hr.noctrl.edu . Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
