    "https://northcentralcollege.peopleadmin.com/postings/14995": {
      "title": "Fine Arts Events Student Worker",
      "description": "PeopleAdmin Applicant Portal | Fine Arts Events Student Worker Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities at North Central College Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Fine Arts Events Student Worker Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Federal Work Study Eligible? Yes Posting Number ST001047 Position Title Fine Arts Events Student Worker Department Fine Arts Division Business Affairs Supervisor Jennifer Holloway Supervisor Title Description of Job Duties 1. Interacting with patrons of the college and performing arts events in a professional manner. 2. Contributing to team goals and initiatives by attending student trainings, working collaboratively on projects, and assisting the Fine Arts Venue & Guest Services Manager, Production Manager, Associate Director and the Director of Fine Arts when necessary. 3. Preparing for performing arts and external events by liaising with the supervisor on duty and fulfilling client needs whilst working with the Student Lead and the rest of the team for venue preparation and full event execution. 4. Interacting with volunteer ushers for the department; communicating with and coordinating them in a professional, helpful manner. 5. Attending monthly ‘in-service meetings’ to communicate with the Fine Arts Venue & Guest Services Manager, about programming or season updates, changes, and other important information pertaining to employment. 6. Opening and closing the box office during appropriate shifts, as well as opening and closing the box office for the nights of performances if the Box Office is in use for the event. Fine Arts Event Student Worker North Central College’s Fine & Performing Arts Department is looking for enthusiastic and dedicated Fine Arts Event Student Workers to help bring our vibrant events to life! In this multifaceted role, you’ll gain hands-on experience in event management, customer service, and performance operations across our premier venues, including Pfeiffer Hall, Wentz Concert Hall, the Theatre at Meiley-Swallow Hall, and Madden Theatre. If you’re a team player with a knack for organization and a passion for the arts, we encourage you to apply! What You’ll Do: Event Set-Up & Support: Efficiently set up and break down event equipment, including tables, chairs, and other necessary items for various performances and events. Assist external groups utilizing college property for their events, ensuring safe practices and adherence to contract specifications and logistics. Help with other event management tasks as needed, adapting to the unique characteristics of each event. Box Office & Patron Services: Opportunity for advancement into the box office desk shifts through training and assessment. Process and sell tickets for performances using our online ticketing system, assisting patrons in person, over the phone, and with online orders. Serve as a primary point of contact for patrons and guests, answering questions, providing directions, and ensuring a positive experience. Prepare for events by organizing “will call” tickets and setting up for ticket sales. Open and close the box office for shifts and performances as required. Front-of-House & Coordination: Assist with communicating professionally with volunteer ushers, including managing sign-ups and night of show coordination. Help manage event attendees and maintain a welcoming and organized environment in the performance venues. Serve as a distinguished and professional representative of North Central College at all events. Team Collaboration & Training: Contribute to team goals and initiatives by actively participating in student trainings and working collaboratively on projects. Assist department staff as needed to ensure smooth operations. This is an excellent opportunity to gain practical experience in arts administration and event production. Ready to be a part of the magic? Do the job duties for this position include any driving requirements? No Job Qualifications · Must be enrolled as a student at North Central College · Requires high level of professionalism and customer service. Position requires day, night, and weekend hours to accommodate the performance schedule What You’ll Bring: · Availability: Must be available to work some night and weekend hours to accommodate performance schedules (typically a minimum of 2-3 events per month). Box office desk shifts require a further 2 hours weekly dedicated to shifts available during business hour, in addition to the 2-3 events per month minimum. Summer availability is preferred, though not required. · Customer Service: A strong commitment to delivering a high level of professionalism and excellent customer service, including event appropriate attire, which can be made available through assistance from the campus closet as needed. · Technical Skills: Computer proficiency is necessary, with a keen eye for detail. · Team Player: Ability to work effectively as part of a team, take initiative, and adapt to varying event needs. · Reliability: Punctual and dependable, ready to assist with a variety of tasks. Will this position be working with minors? Yes Approximate number of work hours per week Varied hours, 3-6 potentially Posting Detail Information EEO Statement North Central College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. North Central College provides reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities where appropriate. If you need reasonable accommodation, please notify the Office of Human Resource. Determinations on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. Open Date 08/21/2025 Close Date Open Until Filled No Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you able to lift at least 25 lbs., with or without an accommodation? Yes No * Are you available to work evenings and weekends? Yes No * Please select the answer that best describes your student work authorization: I am authorized to work for any US employer and can provide documentation, if hired. I am an international student with a US social security number authorized for campus work. I am an international student and will need to apply for a US social security number, if hired. I cannot provide US work authorization. * Are you currently enrolled as a North Central College student? Yes No * Please list any previous customer service experience: (Open Ended Question) * What is your current year in school? Freshman Sophomore Junior Senior Graduate student * Please list your college major(s) (Open Ended Question) * Please list your preferred pronouns (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Optional Documents North Central College 30 North Brainard Street, Naperville, IL 60540 630.637.5757 humanresources@hr.noctrl.edu . Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://northcentralcollege.peopleadmin.com/postings/14977": {
      "title": "Adjunct for Occupational Therapy Department",
      "description": "PeopleAdmin Applicant Portal | Adjunct for Occupational Therapy Department Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities at North Central College Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Adjunct for Occupational Therapy Department Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F000401 Position Title Adjunct for Occupational Therapy Department Department Occupational Therapy Division Academic Affairs Faculty Status Per Course Part-time Faculty Supervisor Title Chair, Department of Occupational Therapy Status Per Course Part-time Faculty Tenure Track No Salary Range 5775 Position Summary The Occupational Therapy program at North Central College invites applications for adjunct faculty positions. Candidates must have a minimum of master’s degree (Doctorate degree preferred) and be licensed as an occupational therapist in the state of Illinois. Courses will be taught both on ground and online. Adjuncts must be able to commit to teaching during the day in person on the campus. Founded in 1861, North Central College is a selective, comprehensive liberal arts institution of about 3000 students, located 28 miles west of Chicago in Naperville. The college is within walking distance of the Naperville Metra station and is next to downtown Naperville. The Naperville area is home to many excellent school districts and Naperville, IL has been ranked as one of the best places to live by Money magazine. For more information, please visit: http://www.noctrl.edu . Interested candidates should submit an application with their curriculum vitae and cover letter using the following link: https://northcentralcollege.peopleadmin.com/postings/13518 . For further information, please email Dr. Michelle Sheperd, Program Director, at msheperd@noctrl.edu. Review of applications begins immediately and will be on an ongoing continuous basis to create a substantial pool of applicants for current and future adjunct positions. North Central College is an EEO Employer. Employment Conditions An offer of employment is contingent upon successful completion of the College’s background screening process. Number of Vacancies 1 Posting Detail Information EEO Statement North Central College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. NCC provides reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities where appropriate. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application or hiring process, please notify the Office of Human Resources at 630-637-5757 or humanresources@hr.noctrl.edu Determinations for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Additional Information Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you authorized to work in the US? YES NO * Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for work authorization? YES NO Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Optional Documents Teaching Philosophy North Central College 30 North Brainard Street, Naperville, IL 60540 630.637.5757 humanresources@hr.noctrl.edu . Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://northcentralcollege.peopleadmin.com/postings/14919": {
      "title": "Adjunct Pool - Spanish Instructor",
      "description": "PeopleAdmin Applicant Portal | Adjunct Pool - Spanish Instructor Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities at North Central College Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Adjunct Pool - Spanish Instructor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F000439 Position Title Adjunct Pool - Spanish Instructor Department World Languages & Cultures Division College of Arts & Sciences Faculty Status Per Course Part-time Faculty Supervisor Title Chair, World Languages and Cultures Status Per Course Part-time Faculty Tenure Track No Salary Range $3,840 to $4,380 Position Summary The Department of World Languages and Cultures in the College of Arts and Sciences at North Central College invites applications for an adjunct, non-tenure track position in Spanish. Adjunct faculty are appointed on a course-by-course basis. This posting is ongoing to develop a qualified pool of candidates. If your academic area of interest, graduate degree work, and professional experience meet our programmatic needs at any time through the academic year, you may be contacted to discuss teaching opportunities. The department needs vary from semester to semester. The duties in this role include: Deliver communicative instruction following the provided syllabus and textbook, for a variety of sections in elementary and intermediate Spanish courses. Assess students’ work and provide detailed feedback on how to improve students’ oral and written communication skills in Spanish. Report midterm and final grades to Registrar within the college due dates and platforms. Communicate regularly and timely with the Elementary Spanish Coordinator and the World Languages and Cultures Chair about the general development of the courses and/or any issues that may arise. Basic Qualifications: The successful candidate will have completed a Masters or Ph.D. degree in Spanish, Linguistics, Literature or related fields. The qualified individual should demonstrate high-advanced, native-like, or native fluency in Spanish at the oral and written levels. Applicants must demonstrate commitment to excellence in teaching and mentoring of students, and ongoing scholarship. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with teaching Spanish, Linguistics or Literature. Demonstrated excellence in communication skills, teaching, and research. Salary Range: The budgeted salary range for this position is $3,840 to $4,380 per 4 credit hour course. About NCC : Founded in 1861, North Central College is a selective, comprehensive liberal arts institution of about 3000 students, located 28 miles west of Chicago in Naperville. The College is in a period of growth with the addition of a $60 million Science Center (2017), and a new Health Sciences and Engineering building (2020). The college is within walking distance of the Naperville Metra station and is next to downtown Naperville. The Naperville area is home to many excellent school districts and Naperville, IL has been ranked as one of the best places to live by Money magazine. North Central College values diversity, equity and inclusion and strongly encourages candidates who would enrich the diversity of the campus community to apply. Experience working with diverse student populations and communities is highly desirable. For more information, please visit: https://www.northcentralcollege.edu/academic-affairs/prospective-and-incoming-faculty . Interested candidates should complete and submit an application with all required documentation online at: https://northcentralcollege.peopleadmin.com/postings/14729 . For further information, contact Patricia Bayona-Chavarro, Chair, Department of World Languages and Cultures, at pbayona@noctrl.edu. Employment Conditions An offer of employment is contingent upon successful completion of the College’s background screening process. Number of Vacancies 1 Posting Detail Information EEO Statement North Central College is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to increasing the diversity of our workforce. North Central College provides reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities where appropriate. If you need reasonable accommodation, please notify the Office of Human Resource. Determinations on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Additional Information The budgeted salary range for this position is $3,840 to $4,380 per 4-credit hour course . The pay offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors including (but not limited to) the selected candidate’s experience and qualifications, including equivalent years in rank, training, and field or discipline; internal equity; and external market pay for comparable jobs. Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you authorized to work in the US? YES NO * Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for work authorization? YES NO Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Contact Information for 3 Professional References Cover Letter/Letter of Interest with discussion around teaching philosophy Optional Documents North Central College 30 North Brainard Street, Naperville, IL 60540 630.637.5757 humanresources@hr.noctrl.edu . Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://northcentralcollege.peopleadmin.com/postings/14913": {
      "title": "Adjunct Pool for School of Business and Entrepreneurship",
      "description": "PeopleAdmin Applicant Portal | Adjunct Pool for School of Business and Entrepreneurship Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities at North Central College Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Adjunct Pool for School of Business and Entrepreneurship Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F000427 Position Title Adjunct Pool for School of Business and Entrepreneurship Department School of Business & Entrepreneurship Division Academic Affairs Faculty Status Per Course Part-time Faculty Supervisor Title CHAIR, Department of Economics & Finance Status Per Course Part-time Faculty Tenure Track No Salary Range $1,920-$4,520 Position Summary The School of Business and Entrepreneurship at North Central College invites applications for an adjunct pool in the School of Business and Entrepreneurship. Adjunct faculty are appointed on a course-by-course basis. This posting is ongoing to develop a qualified pool of candidates. If your academic area of interest, graduate degree work, and professional experience meet our programmatic needs at any time through the academic year, you may be contacted to discuss teaching opportunities. The department needs vary from semester to semester. Courses are offered in Accounting, Business, Business Law, Business Statistics, Economics, Entrepreneurship, Finance, Human Resource Management, International Business, Management, Marketing, Operations and Supply Chain Management, and Leadership. Undergraduate courses are delivered primarily in-person across a 16-week semester (fall or spring) with a limited number of online (synchronous or asynchronous courses). Graduate courses in the MBA program are delivered online asynchronous format in 6 or 8 weeks. The adjunct faculty role requires someone who can deliver course content, contribute to the creation of assignments and other assessments, evaluate and grade student work, and hold office hours to assist students. Minimum qualifications include a graduate degree in the field related to teaching such as an MBA or Master’s Degree and meet the qualification requirements for AACSB including recent work experience in the discipline or other professional engagement. Preferred qualifications included college-level teaching experience or a doctoral degree. Successful candidates will have demonstrated commitment to teaching excellence. Founded in 1861, North Central College is a nationally recognized institution of about 3000 students, located in Naperville, IL, a thriving suburb just west of Chicago. The College is in a period of growth with the addition of a $60 million Science Center (2017), and a new Health Sciences and Engineering building (2020). North Central College is within walking distance of the Naperville Metra station and is next to downtown Naperville. The Naperville area is home to many excellent school districts and Naperville, IL has been ranked as one of the best places to live by Money magazine. For more information, please visit: http://www.noctrl.edu . North Central College is an EEO Employer. Interested candidates should complete an application, submit a cover letter that discusses teaching philosophy as well as a resume/CV, and a copy of unofficial transcripts in an electronic format to: https://northcentralcollege.peopleadmin.com/postings/14628 . For further information, please contact: Sarah Kostelny, Chair, Accounting Department (sskostelny@noctrl.edu Gwendolyn Tedeschi, Chair, Economics & Finance (gatedeschi@noctrl.edu) Mary Galvan, Chair, Management & Marketing (mtgalvan@noctrl.edu) Julie Nagashima, Director, Leadership, Ethics, & Values Program (jnagashima@noctrl.edu) • At this time, we are only able to hire employees who reside in the following states: Arizona, Colorado, Illinois, Indiana, New York, North Carolina, Oregon, Pennsylvania, and Wisconsin. Employment Conditions An offer of employment is contingent upon successful completion of the College’s background screening process. Number of Vacancies 1 Posting Detail Information EEO Statement North Central College is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to increasing the diversity of our workforce. North Central College provides reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities where appropriate. If you need reasonable accommodation, please notify the Office of Human Resource. Determinations on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Additional Information The budgeted salary range for this position is $1,920 – $4,520. The pay offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors including (but not limited to) the selected candidate’s experience and qualifications, including equivalent years in rank, training, and field or discipline; internal equity; and class credit hours. Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you authorized to work in the US? YES NO * Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for work authorization? YES NO Applicant Documents Required Documents Unofficial Graduate Transcripts Resume or Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Interest with discussion around teaching philosophy Optional Documents North Central College 30 North Brainard Street, Naperville, IL 60540 630.637.5757 humanresources@hr.noctrl.edu . Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://northcentralcollege.peopleadmin.com/postings/14613": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor for Accounting",
      "description": "PeopleAdmin Applicant Portal | Adjunct Instructor for Accounting Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities at North Central College Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Adjunct Instructor for Accounting Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F000426 Position Title Adjunct Instructor for Accounting Department Accounting Division Academic Affairs Faculty Status Per Course Part-time Faculty Supervisor Title Chair, Department of Accounting Status Per Course Part-time Faculty Tenure Track No Salary Range $3,800-$4,100 Position Summary The Department of Accounting in the School of Business and Entrepreneurship at North Central College invites applications for an adjunct instructor (non tenure-track) to teach undergraduate financial accounting or managerial accounting for fall 2025 or spring 2026 semester. Candidates may be assigned to one or more courses. Minimum qualifications include a master’s degree in accounting and related work experience related to the area of teaching. College-level teaching experience, advanced degrees, or certifications are preferred but not required. Successful candidates must demonstrate a commitment to teaching excellence. Founded in 1861, North Central College is a nationally recognized institution of about 3000 students, located in Naperville, IL, a thriving suburb just west of Chicago. The College is in a period of growth with the addition of a $60 million Science Center (2017), and a new Health Sciences and Engineering building (2020). North Central College is within walking distance of the Naperville Metra station and is next to downtown Naperville. The Naperville area is home to many excellent school districts and Naperville, IL has been ranked as one of the best places to live by Money magazine. For more information, please visit: http://www.noctrl.edu . North Central College is an EEO Employer. Interested candidates should complete an application and submit a cover letter addressing teaching philosophy, curriculum vitae, and unofficial transcripts in an electronic format to: https://northcentralcollege.peopleadmin.com/postings/14612 . For further information, contact Professor Sarah Kostelny, Chair, Accounting, at sskostelny@noctrl.edu. Review of applications will begin and continue until the position is filled. Employment Conditions An offer of employment is contingent upon successful completion of the College’s background screening process. Number of Vacancies 1 Posting Detail Information EEO Statement North Central College is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to increasing the diversity of our workforce. North Central College provides reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities where appropriate. If you need reasonable accommodation, please notify the Office of Human Resource. Determinations on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Additional Information The budgeted salary range for this position is $3,800 to $4,100. The pay offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors including (but not limited to) the selected candidate’s experience and qualifications, including equivalent years in rank, training, and field or discipline; internal equity; and external market pay for comparable jobs. Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you authorized to work in the US? YES NO * Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for work authorization? YES NO Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Graduate Transcripts Cover Letter/Letter of Interest with discussion around teaching philosophy Optional Documents North Central College 30 North Brainard Street, Naperville, IL 60540 630.637.5757 humanresources@hr.noctrl.edu . Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
