    "https://northcentralcollege.peopleadmin.com/postings/14543": {
      "title": "LRC Student Assistant",
      "description": "PeopleAdmin Applicant Portal | LRC Student Assistant Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities at North Central College Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help LRC Student Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Federal Work Study Eligible? Posting Number ST000932 Position Title LRC Student Assistant Department World Languages and Cultures Division College of Arts & Sciences Supervisor Dr. Patricia Bayona Supervisor Title Associate Professor of Spanish, Director of the Language Resource Center, Coordinator of Elementary Spanish Description of Job Duties LRC Student Assistants will staff the “open” hours of the Language Resource Center ( LRC ) for 2-10 hours per week and assist department faculty and students in the in the preparation or completion of language-learning/teaching projects using a variety of technologies. Do the job duties for this position include any driving requirements? No Job Qualifications Minimum: Enrolled as a student at North Central College. Name and email of an NCC professor willing to provide a reference testifying to your competency and professional behavior on campus. Aptitude for learning language-learning/teaching technologies. Excellent customer service skills. Preferred: Majoring in one of the Modern or Classical Languages at North Central College. Application Requirements Upload a resume to this online application. If you need assistance in the creation of a resume or cover letter, please contact the Center for Career and Professional Development at career@noctrl.edu or 630-637-5141. The NCC faculty reference will receive an email request with a link to upload their statement testifying to your competency in the faculty’s subject area. Applications without this faculty reference will be considered incomplete and not qualified. Will this position be working with minors? No Approximate number of work hours per week 2-6 Posting Detail Information EEO Statement North Central College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. NCC provides reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities where appropriate. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application or hiring process, please notify the Office of Human Resources at 630-637-5757 or humanresources@hr.noctrl.edu Determinations for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. Open Date 05/13/2025 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please select the answer that best describes your student work authorization: I am authorized to work for any US employer and can provide documentation, if hired. I am an international student with a US social security number authorized for campus work. I am an international student and will need to apply for a US social security number, if hired. I cannot provide US work authorization. * Are you currently enrolled as a North Central College student? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents North Central College 30 North Brainard Street, Naperville, IL 60540 630.637.5757 humanresources@hr.noctrl.edu . Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://northcentralcollege.peopleadmin.com/postings/14474": {
      "title": "English Language Institute Student Worker",
      "description": "PeopleAdmin Applicant Portal | English Language Institute Student Worker Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities at North Central College Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help English Language Institute Student Worker Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Federal Work Study Eligible? Posting Number ST000930 Position Title English Language Institute Student Worker Department English Language Institute Division Academic Affairs Supervisor Katherine Pope Supervisor Title Director, English Language Institute Description of Job Duties Assist in maintaining social media accounts for the English Language Institute ( ELI ). Assist with programming for the English Language Institute, as appropriate. Responsibilities may include assisting with the coordination of ELI activities, orientations, and end of term celebrations. Assist the ELI Director with current and prospective student communication. Assist with coordinating student arrival and orientation. Assist in maintaining ELI student files, programmatic resources and databases. Liaise with campus offices such as Residence Life, Registrar, International Admission, and the Dyson Wellness Center, as needed. Greet current and prospective ELI students in a professional manner. Ability to maintain confidentiality. Perform general office duties such as filing, creating labels and making copies. Do the job duties for this position include any driving requirements? Yes Job Qualifications Minimum: Currently enrolled as a North Central College student in good academic standing. Show strong attention to detail and ability to manage time efficiently. Ability to communicate with staff, faculty, students, and community members in a clear, professional, and friendly manner. Ability to problem solve and use critical thinking skills. Basic computer skills in programs such as Microsoft 365, Outlook, and Adobe and be comfortable working with data and completing office processes using the computer. Ability to work in databases and spreadsheets and enter data with minimal error. Preferred: Valid driver’s license and acceptable driving record Will this position be working with minors? Yes Approximate number of work hours per week 3-10 Posting Detail Information EEO Statement North Central College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. NCC provides reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities where appropriate. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application or hiring process, please notify the Office of Human Resources at 630-637-5757 or humanresources@hr.noctrl.edu Determinations for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. Open Date 04/25/2025 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently enrolled as a North Central College student? Yes No * Please select the answer that best describes your student work authorization: I am authorized to work for any US employer and can provide documentation, if hired. I am an international student with a US social security number authorized for campus work. I am an international student and will need to apply for a US social security number, if hired. I cannot provide US work authorization. * What is your current year in school? Freshman Sophomore Junior Senior Graduate * What is your work availability? (Open Ended Question) * Please describe the characteristics and/or skills you already possess that will assist you in this position. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Optional Documents North Central College 30 North Brainard Street, Naperville, IL 60540 630.637.5757 humanresources@hr.noctrl.edu . Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://northcentralcollege.peopleadmin.com/postings/14331": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor for Accounting",
      "description": "PeopleAdmin Applicant Portal | Adjunct Instructor for Accounting Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities at North Central College Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Adjunct Instructor for Accounting Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F000394 Position Title Adjunct Instructor for Accounting Department Accounting Division Academic Affairs Faculty Status Per Course Part-time Faculty Supervisor Title Chair, Department of Accounting Status Per Course Part-time Faculty Tenure Track No Salary Range $3,800-$4,100 Position Summary The Department of Accounting in the School of Business and Entrepreneurship at North Central College invites applications for an adjunct professor non tenure-track to teach two undergraduate courses: (1) an in-person Managerial Accounting course and (2) an in-person Cost Accounting course. Both courses begin January 6th and end April 30th. Candidates can either teach one or both courses. ACCT 202: Managerial Accounting – M/W/F 2:40-3:45pm (One day a week can be held remotely) ACCT 307: Cost Accounting – M/W/F 1:20-2:25pm (One day a week can be held remotely) Candidates possessing a doctoral degree are preferred but candidates with a master’s degree and college-level teaching experience are also encouraged to apply. Successful candidates will have demonstrated commitment to teaching excellence. North Central College values diversity, equity and inclusion and strongly encourages candidates who would enrich the diversity of the campus community to apply. Experience working with diverse student populations and communities is highly desirable. Founded in 1861, North Central College is a nationally recognized institution of about 3000 students, located in Naperville, IL, a thriving suburb just west of Chicago. The College is in a period of growth with the addition of a $60 million Science Center (2017), and a new Health Sciences and Engineering building (2020). North Central College is within walking distance of the Naperville Metra station and is next to downtown Naperville. The Naperville area is home to many excellent school districts and Naperville, IL has been ranked as one of the best places to live by Money magazine. For more information, please visit: http://www.noctrl.edu . Interested candidates should complete an Application, submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy and contact information for three professional references in an electronic format to: https://northcentralcollege.peopleadmin.com/postings/13310 For further information, contact Professor Sarah Kostelny, Chair, Accounting, at sskostelny@noctrl.edu. Review of applications will begin and continue until the position is filled. North Central College is an EEO Employer. Employment Conditions An offer of employment is contingent upon successful completion of the College’s background screening process. Number of Vacancies 1 Posting Detail Information EEO Statement North Central College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. NCC provides reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities where appropriate. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application or hiring process, please notify the Office of Human Resources at 630-637-5757 or humanresources@hr.noctrl.edu Determinations for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Additional Information Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you authorized to work in the US? YES NO * Will you now or in the future require sponsorship for work authorization? YES NO Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Interest with discussion around teaching philosophy Optional Documents North Central College 30 North Brainard Street, Naperville, IL 60540 630.637.5757 humanresources@hr.noctrl.edu . Back to top To 