    "https://northcentralcollege.peopleadmin.com/postings/14190": {
      "title": "Chemistry Laboratory Assistant-student position",
      "description": "PeopleAdmin Applicant Portal | Chemistry Laboratory Assistant-student position Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities at North Central College Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Chemistry Laboratory Assistant-student position Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Federal Work Study Eligible? Posting Number ST000692 Position Title Chemistry Laboratory Assistant-student position Department Chemistry/Physics Division College of Arts & Sciences Supervisor Christopher Gierek Supervisor Title Chemistry - Physics Laboratory Manager/Chemical Hygiene Officer Description of Job Duties The Chemistry Laboratory Assistant assists the Laboratory Manager with the preparation of chemistry laboratory kits, including apparatus set-up and solutions preparations. The Laboratory Assistant maintains and restocks the laboratory chemicals and equipment stock and maintains/cleans laboratory glassware stock. Do the job duties for this position include any driving requirements? No Job Qualifications The successful applicant will have completed the lecture and laboratory coursework of Chemistry 141 and 142 with a letter grade of “C” or higher and be enrolled in Organic Chemistry lecture and lab or have already completed the series of courses with a letter grade of “C” or higher. The applicant should have a basic knowledge of laboratory glassware and equipment in addition to being able to demonstrate the safe and proper handling of chemicals and laboratory equipment. The successful Laboratory Assistant works well in a group setting but can also work independently and without direct supervision. Good verbal and written communication skills are a plus. Will this position be working with minors? No Approximate number of work hours per week 5-15 Posting Detail Information EEO Statement North Central College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. NCC provides reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities where appropriate. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application or hiring process, please notify the Office of Human Resources at 630-637-5757 or humanresources@hr.noctrl.edu Determinations for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. Open Date 01/10/2022 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently enrolled as a North Central College student? Yes No * Please select the answer that best describes your student work authorization: I am authorized to work for any US employer and can provide documentation, if hired. I am an international student with a US social security number authorized for campus work. I am an international student and will need to apply for a US social security number, if hired. I cannot provide US work authorization. * Have you completed the lecture and laboratory coursework of Chemistry 141 and 142 with a letter grade of “C” or higher? Yes No * Are you currently enrolled in Organic Chemistry lecture and lab earning a letter grade of \"C\" or higher, or have you already completed the series of courses and received a letter grade of “C” or higher? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents North Central College 30 North Brainard Street, Naperville, IL 60540 630.637.5757 humanresources@hr.noctrl.edu . Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://northcentralcollege.peopleadmin.com/postings/14146": {
      "title": "Cardinal Fleet Support",
      "description": "PeopleAdmin Applicant Portal | Cardinal Fleet Support Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities at North Central College Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Cardinal Fleet Support Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Federal Work Study Eligible? Posting Number ST001012 Position Title Cardinal Fleet Support Department Campus Safety Division Business Affairs Supervisor Mary Frances Koyl Supervisor Title Assistant Director of Campus Safety Description of Job Duties · Perform vehicle maintenance inspections to determine exterior and interior damages. · Complete a safety inspection of fleet vehicles. · Operate vehicles in the fleet by driving them to refuel, charge the vehicle batteries, and to complete intra/interstate vehicle inspections. · Complete interior vehicle cleanings when necessary. Other duties as assigned. Do the job duties for this position include any driving requirements? Yes Job Qualifications · Must be enrolled as a student at North Central College · Valid US Driver’s License · A minimum (3) years of driving experience · Must successfully complete a driving history background check · Must be vehicle accident free Will this position be working with minors? No Approximate number of work hours per week 5 Posting Detail Information EEO Statement North Central College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. NCC provides reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities where appropriate. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application or hiring process, please notify the Office of Human Resources at 630-637-5757 or humanresources@hr.noctrl.edu Determinations for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. Open Date 05/02/2024 Close Date Open Until Filled No Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please select the answer that best describes your student work authorization: I am authorized to work for any US employer and can provide documentation, if hired. I am an international student with a US social security number authorized for campus work. I am an international student and will need to apply for a US social security number, if hired. I cannot provide US work authorization. * Are you available to work in the summer? Yes No * Are you available to work during winter/spring break? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Work Availability Optional Documents North Central College 30 North Brainard Street, Naperville, IL 60540 630.637.5757 humanresources@hr.noctrl.edu . Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
