    "https://northcentralcollege.peopleadmin.com/postings/14131": {
      "title": "Box Office Student Lead",
      "description": "PeopleAdmin Applicant Portal | Box Office Student Lead Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities at North Central College Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Box Office Student Lead Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Federal Work Study Eligible? Posting Number ST000955 Position Title Box Office Student Lead Department Fine Arts Division Business Affairs Supervisor Jennifer Holloway Supervisor Title Description of Job Duties In addition to the standard tasks of a Box Office Student Worker, this position assists with coordinating student staff and ushers, ticket sales and running of front of house operations for events managed by the Department of Fine & Performing Arts. Work locations are Pfeiffer Hall, the Wentz Concert Hall, the Theatre at Meiley-Swallow Hall, and Madden Theatre. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: 1. Assist with onboarding new box office student workers, such as training, conducting secondary interviews with those chosen by management, etc. 2. Compile the desk shift schedule and implement it into Sling, as instructed by management. 3. Serve as a Day of Show point-person to other student workers as well as to patrons. 4. Coordinate and communicate with volunteer ushers in a professional manner, such as arranging the usher sign-ups, and emailing the ushers with any announcements or reminders. 5. Process and sell tickets for performances through online ticketing system with customers in person, on the phone, or by processing online orders. 6. Interact with event patrons in a professional manner. 7. Contribute to team goals and initiatives by attending student trainings, working collaboratively on projects, and assist department staff as needed. 8. Prepare for performing arts events by prepping will call, ticket sales, usher sign-ins, and/or venue set-up. 9. Attend and assist with the coordination of monthly ‘in-service meetings’ to communicate with department staff about programming or season updates, changes, and other important information pertaining to employment. 10. Open and close the box office during appropriate shifts, and for performances. Do the job duties for this position include any driving requirements? No Job Qualifications Currently employed as a North Central College Box Office Student Worker. Have completed at least 1 year in the position of North Central College Box Office Student Worker. Ability to deliver a high level of professionalism and customer service. Computer proficiency is necessary, along with excellent attention to detail. Available to work some night and weekend hours to accommodate the performance schedule (usually, a minimum of 2-3 events per month). Summer availability is preferred, though not required. Will this position be working with minors? No Approximate number of work hours per week 10-20 Posting Detail Information EEO Statement North Central College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. NCC provides reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities where appropriate. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application or hiring process, please notify the Office of Human Resources at 630-637-5757 or humanresources@hr.noctrl.edu Determinations for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. Open Date 10/18/2022 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently enrolled as a North Central College student? Yes No * Have you worked as a NCC Box Office Student Worker for least 1 academic year? Yes No * Please describe a time you went above and beyond in your role as Box Office Student Worker (Open Ended Question) * Please list your college major(s) (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Optional Documents North Central College 30 North Brainard Street, Naperville, IL 60540 630.637.5757 humanresources@hr.noctrl.edu . Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
