    "https://northcentralcollege.peopleadmin.com/postings/14123": {
      "title": "Coffee Lab Student Assistant",
      "description": "PeopleAdmin Applicant Portal | Coffee Lab Student Assistant Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities at North Central College Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Coffee Lab Student Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Federal Work Study Eligible? Posting Number ST000934 Position Title Coffee Lab Student Assistant Department Management/Marketing Division Academic Affairs Supervisor Amy Rogers Supervisor Title Coffee Lab Operations Manager Description of Job Duties We offer a fun environment, flexible scheduling, and lots of free, fabulous, coffee! Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Coffee Packaging. Assist with the preparation and delivery of brewed coffee on-campus. Assist with on-campus Coffee Hours hosted by the Coffee Lab. Provide tours of the Coffee Lab to visitors. Oversee the on-campus Coffee Lab / Enactus store during work hours. Clean and stock the lab and store. Each student assistant will also be assigned to one of the following roles: Online Orders Responsible for making sure all online orders are fulfilled. This includes checking the website on a daily basis, packaging orders to go out on a regular schedule (minimum of 2 X per week), and arranging for the shipping and/or pick-up of the orders. Hours flexible. Coffee Catering Service Assist with coordination of the various coffee catering services provided on-campus. This includes communicating with customers, working closely with additional volunteers including Enactus team members and CEL students, and arranging the preparation, delivery, and clean-up of the coffee services. Hours are flexible but will also be determined by catering schedule. Assistant Store Manager Assist in overseeing the onsite store including working closely with additional volunteers including Enactus team members and CEL students to make sure weekly hours are fulfilled as well as assist with product inventory, display, and promotion. Hours flexible. Sunday Morning Service Oversee the fulfillment of an on-going Sunday morning coffee service order. Responsibilities will include preparing the coffee for pick-up and cleaning up the coffee containers when returned. Regular Sunday morning availability required. Do the job duties for this position include any driving requirements? No Job Qualifications Minimum: Currently enrolled as a North Central College student in good academic standing. Show strong attention to detail and ability to manage time efficiently. Ability to communicate with staff, faculty, students, and community members in a clear, professional, and friendly manner. Ability to problem solve and use critical thinking skills. Basic computer skills Will this position be working with minors? No Approximate number of work hours per week 5-20 Posting Detail Information EEO Statement North Central College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. NCC provides reasonable accommodation to applicants with disabilities where appropriate. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application or hiring process, please notify the Office of Human Resources at 630-637-5757 or humanresources@hr.noctrl.edu Determinations for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. Open Date 01/18/2024 Close Date Open Until Filled No Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently enrolled as a North Central College student? Yes No * Please select the answer that best describes your student work authorization: I am authorized to work for any US employer and can provide documentation, if hired. I am an international student with a US social security number authorized for campus work. I am an international student and will need to apply for a US social security number, if hired. I cannot provide US work authorization. * What is your work availability? (Open Ended Question) * Please describe the characteristics and/or skills you already possess that will assist you in this position. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume North Central College 30 North Brainard Street, Naperville, IL 60540 630.637.5757 humanresources@hr.noctrl.edu . Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
